lowing original-formula summaries retain meaningful differences from the earlier generated handbooks. Source-local SRC numbers refer to S163\u8217?s own source register. They are not this edition\u8217?s S001\u8211?S179 identifiers. The instruction to remove improver overrides earlier suggestions to use it. These are research records, not instructions to add an improver.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V01 \u8212? Agege bread and tangzhong milk bread\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC03/SRC04. Agege, flour basis: flour 100%; water 55\u8211?58%; sugar 10\u8211?12%; fat 8\u8211?10%; instant yeast 1.5\u8211?2%; salt 1.5%; improver 0.5% as an unverified original entry. Use the actual improver supplier dose, not the generic percentage. Original starting method: mix 3 minutes low, 8\u8211?10 minutes faster; proof to expansion; bake near 180\u176?C for 25\u8211?30 minutes. Piece mass, tin size, dough temperature and finished yield are missing. Retain the dense, stretchy style as a separate trial from S-B02.\par \pard\sa120 Shokupan original: tangzhong flour 7% plus liquid 35%; main dough flour 93%, milk 50%, sugar 10%, butter 10%, egg 10%, instant yeast 1.5%, salt 1.2%. The roux liquid plus main milk totals 85% of flour before egg if both are additional. It is unclear whether the 50% milk includes the roux liquid. Resolve this before mixing; do not silently reduce liquid or present the formula as verified. Baking, portion and pan specifications are also absent. Softness claims are not shelf-life evidence.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V02 \u8212? Specialist bread and pastry archive\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 These formula records come from SRC16 and the related SRC17/SRC19 drafts; SRC05/SRC14 later summarized them. Amounts below are original batch quantities unless percentages are stated. Butter, margarine and shortening are distinct ingredients requiring an explicit choice.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Product\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Retained formula or distinctive variant\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Development decision\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Plain butter biscuits\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; powdered sugar 7.2 kg; butter/margarine 9 kg; egg 1.8 kg; milk powder 540 g; vanilla 90 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct from S-P04 coconut biscuits. Confirm fat, portion, mixing and water activity; reject six-month life claim.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Croissant\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water/milk 9.9 kg with split unspecified; sugar 1.98 kg; dough butter 720 g; salt 360 g; yeast 270 g; roll-in butter 4.5 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Other drafts use 9.72 kg water, 900 g dough fat and different roll-in percentages. Select one formula; do not combine them. Confirm lamination equipment, fat plasticity and proof conditions.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pain au chocolat\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Croissant base; 10\u8211?12 g chocolate per pastry in one version; two batons in another\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Define baton mass and dough weight. Pilot 4 mm sheet and 8 \u215? 12 cm rectangles only after the base is fixed.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pound cake\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; sugar 18 kg; fat 18 kg; egg 16.2 kg; baking powder 270 g; salt 90 g; flavour 100 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Another draft has 18 kg egg and 360 g baking powder. Select a fixed version, edible egg mass, tin fill and mixing method; use a creaming-capable mixer.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Hard dough loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water 8.64 kg; sugar 1.26 kg; shortening 1.08 kg; salt 360 g; instant yeast 108 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Other versions differ materially in water, sugar and fat. Validate dense-dough load and moulder limits; do not force tight rollers.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pain aux raisins\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Croissant dough; 2.5 kg raisins per 18 kg flour; pastry cream unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Incomplete: define cream recipe, quantity, treatment and chilled handling.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Vend\u233?enne-style braid\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; sugar 3.24 kg; butter 4.5 kg; egg 5.4 kg; water 1.8 kg; salt 360 g; yeast 360 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 A 25%-butter variant, distinct from S-B06 50%-butter brioche. Regional naming needs care; validate cold fermentation and shaping.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Long sandwich roll\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water 10.8 kg; sugar 720 g; shortening 720 g; salt 360 g; instant yeast 144 g; malt 54 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Define malt type and activity. Original 150 g dough piece is a pilot size, not final label mass.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut crunch bread\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water 9.36 kg; sugar 2.7 kg; margarine 1.44 kg; coconut 1.8 kg; salt 270 g; yeast 180 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Topping quantity absent; specify coconut moisture and topping before costing.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Whole-wheat loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Whole-wheat flour 9 kg + white flour 9 kg; water 11.7 kg; honey/molasses 900 g; oil 720 g; salt 360 g; yeast 126 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Select honey or molasses. Optional oats/flax not quantified. Compare with V04\u8217?s 60% whole-wheat formula.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Garlic-herb-cheese fougasse\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water 11.16 kg; oil 1.08 kg; garlic 90 g; herbs 54 g; salt 360 g; yeast 90 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Garlic-oil and cheese topping amounts absent. Define yeast type and topping yield.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Laminated sausage roll\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; lamination fat 9 kg; meat filling 15 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Pastry liquid, seasoning and binding missing. O-P08 is a complete shortcrust alternative, not an equivalent laminated formula.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Brownie\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Sugar 14.4 kg; ambiguous \u8220?cocoa margarine\u8221? 9 kg; cocoa 3.6 kg; egg 7.2 kg; flour 5.4 kg; baking powder 54 g; vanilla 50 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Identify fat and tray depth; validate center set and cooled cut yield. Do not approve from surface colour alone.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pain viennoise\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; milk 9.9 kg; sugar 1.44 kg; butter 1.8 kg; salt 360 g; yeast 180 g; optional chocolate 1.8 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct from S-B07 pain au lait. Cost and label the chocolate version separately.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Levain boule\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 18 kg; water 11.7 kg; levain 3.6 kg; salt 360 g; instant yeast 36 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Levain hydration, flour contribution and maturity missing; total hydration cannot be established.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Vanilla gelato\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk 12 kg; cream 3 kg; sugar 3 kg; skim powder 750 g; glucose/dextrose 300 g; vanilla 60 g; stabilizer 90 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Ingredient types/solids and stabilizer unidentified. Prefer S-D02; do not assume a soft-serve machine is a batch freezer.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pineapple-ginger pop\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Juice 14 kg; water 3.5 kg; 65\u176?Brix syrup 2 kg; ginger 450 g; lime 150 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Fruit composition and treatment missing. S-I01 is the more specified trial.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cocoa cream pop\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk 11 kg; water 3 kg; cocoa 1.5 kg; sugar 3.5 kg; \u8220?cornstarch/stabilizer\u8221? 120 g; vanilla 30 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Starch and stabilizer are not interchangeable. Prefer S-I03 or develop a separate specified starch formula.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cocoa-banana gelato\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk 10 kg; banana 4 kg; cocoa 1.5 kg; sugar 2.2 kg; cream 2 kg (SRC15)\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Determine fat/solids, fruit treatment, freezing behaviour, equipment and portions.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Baguette, Kumba, Pullman, burger buns, pain beurre and pain au lait from the same archive map to S-B01\u8211?S-B05 and S-B07. Their earlier ingredient ranges were development versions, not independent approved products. The exact original files remain identified in the source register; the complete S cards are the working specifications.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V03 \u8212? Additional September concepts\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC05/SRC14. These additions retain ideas not fully covered by the later cards.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Product\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Formula retained\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b What must be resolved\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Cocoa-groundnut breakfast loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Bread flour 17.1 kg; roasted groundnut flour 900 g; cocoa 540 g; water or milk 10.8 kg; sugar 1.44 kg; oil 900 g; milk powder 540 g; salt 324 g; instant yeast 180 g; optional chocolate 1.8 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Select water or milk; test absorption, nut quality, allergens and portion yield. Initial 250\u8211?300 g dough, 190\u176?C/18\u8211?22 minutes are trial starting points.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Chicken-vegetable pocket\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Dough: flour 10 kg, water 5.5 kg, sugar 500 g, oil 400 g, salt 180 g, instant yeast 100 g. Filling: cooked chicken 5 kg, cabbage 1 kg, carrot 800 g, onion 800 g, oil 250 g, seasoning 100 g, breadcrumbs or cooked potato 500 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Select binder and seasoning; quantify egg wash and cooked filling loss. Original assembly 60\u8211?70 g dough + 40 g filling; bake trial 195\u8211?205\u176?C/15\u8211?18 minutes with verified core cooking.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Mango \u8220?ginger\u8221? soft serve\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk 5.5 kg; cream 1.2 kg; sugar 1.4 kg; skim powder 600 g; dextrose/glucose 250 g; mango 1 kg; lime 50 g; stabilizer about 50 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 No ginger amount is supplied despite the name. Total is 10.25 kg before adjustments. Select dry sugar type and specified stabilizer; qualify treated fruit additions and machine compatibility.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Early bissap pop\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Water 6.5 kg; infusion 1.5 kg; 65\u176?Brix syrup 1.8 kg; ginger 150 g; lime 50 g; stabilizer 20\u8211?30 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Syrup contributes only 1.17 kg sugar, so the original 18\u8211?22\u176?Brix assertion is not supported by the listed sugars. Use S-I02 as the revised trial.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Shawarma baguette\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Baguette 250 g; cooked chicken 80\u8211?100 g; fries 100\u8211?120 g; sauce 30 g; salad 30\u8211?40 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 A portion-range concept. Fix exact weights and costs using O-B18/O-B20/O-B22/O-B24 and S-B01 before sale.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Spring rolls\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Cabbage 3 kg; carrot 1.2 kg; onion 700 g; optional cooked chicken/beef 2 kg; oil 250 g; garlic/ginger 120 g; seasoning/salt 120 g; optional breadcrumbs/cooked potato 350 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Original target about 100 pieces, with 45\u8211?50 g filling each, purchased wrappers and 170\u8211?175\u176?C frying trial. Define wrapper mass/count, split seasonings, sealing paste, absorbed oil and cooked filling yield; validate the center rather than relying on the original 3\u8211?4-minute time.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Focaccia slab; coconut nondairy frozen dessert; mango/passionfruit/banana fruit trio\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Selection concepts without fully resolved formulas\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Keep on the development list; do not imply a complete recipe was supplied. Rebalance fruit sugar/acid and coconut fat/solids separately.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V04 \u8212? October blueprint alternatives\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC22; SRC23 is an exact duplicate. Values are original commercial batches. These preserve formula alternatives and new concepts without carrying over unsupported machine or life claims. Meat uses H01, dairy H02/H04 and fruit H03; no raw-meat massaging in the dairy tank.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Original product\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Retained ingredients\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Harmonized decision\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Milk sandwich bread\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 50 kg; water 28 L; milk powder 2.5 kg; margarine 2 kg; sugar 3 kg; salt 900 g; yeast 600 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Older milk-powder alternative to O-P01/S-B04; do not assume four-day life.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Hard-crust baguette\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 50 kg; water 31 L; salt 1 kg; yeast 500 g; ascorbic acid 10 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Improver specification and supplier dose required; S-B01 is the clearer working card.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Chin-chin\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 25 kg; sugar 6 kg; margarine 5 kg; milk powder 1.5 kg; nutmeg/vanilla 200 g combined; eggs 30; water 5 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Weigh eggs, split flavour quantities, specify dough thickness and fry endpoint. Three-month life unsupported.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Dual-leavened beignets\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 20 kg; sugar 4 kg; yeast 400 g; baking powder 150 g; salt 200 g; water 13 L; flavour 100 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct from yeast puff-puff and cake beignets. Fix leavener types and test; no guarantee of hollow or oil-free texture.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Powder-milk yogurt\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Full-cream powder 5 kg; water 22 L; sugar 2 kg; YF-L811 culture 5 g; flavour 50 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Culture units, supplier dose, total solids and working tank volume unresolved; do not inherit S-Y culture dosing.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Chicken marinade\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Chicken 20 kg; yogurt 2 L; oil 1 L; garlic 500 g; spices 300 g; lemon 400 ml; salt 250 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Weigh liquids and identify spices; marination is refrigerated and does not replace cooking.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Yogurt-mayo sauce\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Mayonnaise 5.5 L; yogurt 3.5 L; garlic 500 g; lemon 250 ml; vinegar 100 ml; salt/pepper 55 g combined\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 SRC26 splits seasoning into 40 g salt + 15 g pepper and adds mint. Keep refrigerated; final mass/volume unmeasured.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Meat-pie filling\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Beef 4 kg; potato 5 kg; carrot 3 kg; onion 2 kg; starch 500 g; \u8220?seasoning/water\u8221? 6 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Seasoning versus water unresolved. O-B09 provides a complete alternative; no unsupported 40% saving claim.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pie crust\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 15 kg; cold margarine 7.5 kg; salt 200 g; cold water 4.5 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct fat ratio from O-B07; validate short mixing and chilled handling.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Koki corn\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Corn mash 15 kg; palm oil 1.5 L; pepper 100 g; salt 120 g; water 2 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Specify corn solids, grinding, wrap size and validated steaming endpoint. Do not assume scraper aeration.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Ndjansang chilli sauce\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Pepper 5 kg; onion 2 kg; toasted ndjansang 300 g; oil 2 L; garlic/ginger 500 g combined; salt/bouillon 200 g combined\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Split all combined ingredients. Hot bottling and oil separation do not establish ambient safety.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut tarts\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut 6 kg; sugar syrup 4 L; vanilla 50 ml; shortcrust shells 100\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Specify syrup solids and shell mass/formula. Measure oven temperature throughout baking; residual heat is not automatically adequate.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Brioche poulet\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Rich brioche dough 10 kg; cooked chicken filling 5 kg; egg wash 200 ml; sesame 50 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Original assembly 80 g dough + 40 g filling gives 125 units before losses; define the dough/filling versions and actual yield.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Caramel topping\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Sugar 10 kg; glucose 3 kg; water 4 L; cream 2 L; salt 30 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 The original 120\u176?C caramelization claim is inadequate. Use a qualified controlled caramel method and appropriate vessel; dairy sauce is not automatically shelf-stable.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Sugar ring donuts\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 20 kg; sugar 3.5 kg; margarine 1.5 kg; yeast 350 g; water 9.5 L; nutmeg 100 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Salt absent in original; resolve deliberate omission and formula before trial. Sugar coating unquantified.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Ganache rings\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Donut rings 200; dark chocolate 4 kg; cream 3 L; butter 500 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Define cream mass/fat, chocolate type, pickup and chilled handling. No all-day warm holding claim.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 60% whole-wheat loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Whole-wheat flour 30 kg; white flour 20 kg; water 33 L; brown sugar 2 kg; margarine 1.5 kg; salt 900 g; yeast 600 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct from V02 50% version. Hydration is 66%; adjust by measured absorption, not an automatic extra 10%.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Avocado-banana cream\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Avocado 8 kg; banana 4 kg; lime 200 ml; ascorbic acid 15 g; icing sugar 2 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Antibrowning ingredients do not confer shelf stability. Treat as perishable with a qualified process.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Savoury puff-puff\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 15 kg; leeks 1.5 kg; onions 1 kg; yeast 300 g; salt 250 g; water 10 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Saut\u233?/cool vegetables under control, define batter mass/portion and fry endpoint; cooking oil allowance absent.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Akara\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Peeled black-eyed-bean mash 12 kg; onion 1.5 kg; salt 100 g; white pepper 30 g; water 1.5 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Specify mash solids, milling and hydration; validate cooking and aeration with suitable equipment.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V05 \u8212? High-value recipe sheet differences\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC20. These are alternative formulas, not automatic improvements to V04.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Product\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Distinct original quantities\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Gap or correction\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Corn/makabo paste\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Corn or grated makabo 15 kg; palm/vegetable oil 2.5 L; pepper 150 g; water 3 L; salt/bouillon 120 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Corn and makabo are not interchangeable raw materials; makabo needs a separately established preparation/cooking process. Frying or baking cannot be assumed equivalent to steamed koki.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Chin-chin\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 12 kg; sugar 3.5 kg; margarine 2.5 kg; eggs 30; nutmeg 80 g; vanilla 100 ml; water about 2.5 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Record edible egg mass and final hydration. Life requires water-activity, packaging and microbial assessment.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Brioche poulet\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 10 kg; fat 1.5 kg; sugar 1.2 kg; yeast 120 g; salt 150 g; cooked chicken filling 6 kg\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Dough liquid/egg missing. Original 80 g dough + 30 g filling differs from V04; do not blend counts.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Drinking yogurt\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk powder 4.5 kg; water 22 L; sugar 2.2 kg; starter/plain yogurt 500 g; gelatin/pectin 50 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Starter alternatives and gelling agents are not interchangeable. Sugar/additive post-treatment introduction and chilling need redesign.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Vinegar chilli sauce\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Pepper 4 kg; onion 2 kg; garlic 500 g; ndjansang 100 g; oil 1.5 L; vinegar 1 L; salt 80 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Vinegar acidity, final pH and thermal process unspecified; refrigerate under approved process, not an ambient claim.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Sweet milk loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 15 kg; milk powder 600 g; sugar 1.5 kg; yeast 150 g; improver 30 g; water 8.5 L; margarine 800 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Salt missing. Improver label required. Extra softness is not validated life extension.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Meat pie\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 10 kg; shortening 4.5 kg; beef 4 kg; carrot 2 kg; potato 2 kg; spices 150 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Pastry water/salt and filling process loss omitted. Prefer O-P07 until completed.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Dual-leavened beignets\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 12 kg; sugar 2.8 kg; baking powder 100 g; yeast 80 g; vanilla 50 g; nutmeg 30 g; water 7.5 L\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Compare with V04, with each leavener fixed and measurable. Salt omitted in original.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Caramel\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Sugar 8 kg; water 2 L; glucose 1.5 kg; \u8220?cream/margarine\u8221? 2.5 L; salt 40 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Cream and margarine are not interchangeable, and margarine volume is ambiguous. Use heat-safe equipment; adding dairy to caramel causes vigorous bubbling.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Avocado-banana cream\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Avocado 10 kg; banana 4 kg; ascorbic acid 20 g; 65\u176?Brix syrup 2 L; lime 300 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Weigh syrup and specify solids; original 48-hour colour claim is unverified and not a safety period.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V06 \u8212? Condensed-milk collection\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC25. Preserve the condensed-milk concept while specifying brand composition, ingredient masses, treatment and machine compatibility. The primary O-series provides more complete trial formulations for most of these formats.\par \trowd\trgaph70\trhdr\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 \b Product\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Original batch or assembly\b0 \cell \pard\intbl\fs18 \b Decision\b0 \cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Soft-serve mix\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed milk 4.5 kg; milk 6 L; cream 3.5 L; water 6 L; sugar 1 kg; stabilizer 80 g; vanilla 60 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Weigh dairy; identify stabilizer and final solids. O-FBASE1 is the more specified trial.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Yogurt/frozen yogurt\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Milk 12 L; condensed milk 5 kg; water 4 L; starter 200 g; vanilla 40 ml\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Culture identity/dose and fermentation curve absent. Not automatically compatible with a soft-serve machine.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Milky pops\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed milk 6 kg; water 12 L; coconut milk or mango pur\u233?e 3 L; cornstarch 350 g; salt 15 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut and mango are distinct variants; treatment and composition differ.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pita\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 5 kg; water 2.8 L; sugar 120 g; salt 80 g; oil 150 ml; active dry yeast 60 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Active dry yeast requires its own handling; not gram-for-gram instant yeast. Moulder flattening capability unverified.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Meat marinade\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Meat 10 kg; yogurt 1.5 kg; garlic 250 g; vinegar 200 ml; oil 150 ml; salt 90 g; spice 150 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Beef and chicken require separate specifications and cooking records.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Refrigerator pickle concept\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Cucumber 5 kg; water 3 L; vinegar 2 L; sugar 250 g; salt 200 g; garlic 10 cloves\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Vinegar acidity and garlic mass absent; sealed buckets are not an ambient preservation process. Use O-B23.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Ndjansang sauce\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Pepper 2 kg; ndjansang 150 g; garlic 100 g; ginger 100 g; oil 1 L; salt 40 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 No acid control claimed. Treat as a refrigerated perishable sauce.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk burger buns\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 6 kg; condensed milk 800 g; water 2.8 L; butter 500 g; eggs 6; salt 90 g; instant yeast 80 g; sesame unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Weigh egg and sesame/egg wash; use O-B25 as working alternative.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Smash burger\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 One bun, raw beef 120 g, cheese, sauce, pickles and onion\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Toppings unquantified. Original 90-second cook is not a safety endpoint; follow O-P16/H01.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Pain charg\u233? beef filling\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Beef 4 kg; onion 2 kg; garlic/ginger 150 g; oil 300 ml; cabbage 3 kg; pepper/seasoning unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Separate combined ingredients; weigh cooked output and portion.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Chips and pain charg\u233?\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Initial 140\u176?C/5-minute fry, final 180\u176?C/2\u8211?3-minute fry proposed; sandwich adds beef filling 150 g plus chips/sauce unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Potato and plantain need separate trials. Use O-B24 for fries; define bread and all portions.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk sandwich loaf\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 10 kg; condensed milk 1.2 kg; water 5.4 L; shortening 400 g; salt 150 g; yeast 100 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Working alternatives O-P01/O-P02; qualify pan load and finished mass.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk baguette\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 10 kg; condensed milk 300 g; water 5.8 L; salt 180 g; yeast 90 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Distinct enriched bread, not S-B01 lean baguette.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk chin-chin\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 8 kg; margarine 1.5 kg; condensed milk 2 kg; eggs 12; nutmeg 40 g; frying oil unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Edible egg, hydration, oil use and finished yield unresolved.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk puff-puff\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Flour 5 kg; condensed milk 800 g; water 3.2 L; sugar 400 g; yeast 60 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Trial sweetness/proof/fry behaviour; \u8220?oil-free\u8221? claim rejected.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Koki corn\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Corn mash 10 kg; palm oil 1.2 L; pepper 50 g; water 1.5 L; salt 80 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Specify steaming and mash consistency; a scraper does not guarantee aeration.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Condensed-milk caramel\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Sugar 4 kg; condensed milk 2 kg; glucose 1.5 kg; water 1 L; butter 250 g\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Qualify vessel, heat range, controlled dairy addition, chilling and life; no ambient claim.\cell \row \trowd\trgaph70\cellx3333\cellx6667\cellx10000\pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut pastry slices\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Coconut 2 kg + condensed milk 1.5 kg; pastry sheets unspecified\cell \pard\intbl\fs18 Specify sheet formula, mass, pan depth and measured bake program.\cell \row \pard\fs22\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V07 \u8212? Garlic sauce variants\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 Source SRC26. Toum original: peeled garlic 1.5 kg, oil 8 L, lemon juice 450 ml, water 250 ml, salt 70 g. Claimed 10 L yield is unmeasured; weigh inputs, specify oil, blend/emulsify using suitable equipment and determine usable output. A slow scraper is not assumed to make this emulsion. Garlic-in-oil sauce is a perishable product; no ambient storage is authorized.\par \pard\sa120 Yogurt-mayo original: commercial mayonnaise 5.5 L, yogurt 3.5 L, garlic 500 g, lemon 250 ml, vinegar 100 ml, salt 40 g, white pepper 15 g and optional mint 2 tablespoons. Weigh ingredients and mint; verify the mayonnaise and yogurt supply specifications. Keep the cold preparation and service controlled. O-B20 and S-F04 offer smaller fully quantified alternatives with different flavour profiles.\par \pard\sb200\sa140\keepn\b\fs28 V08 \u8212? Brioche format options retained\b0\fs22\par \pard\sa120 SRC05\u8217?s extended brioche uses the same 50%-butter base concept as S-B06 and adds useful alternative shapes. A 5 kg flour batch has 11,450 g raw dough; at an assumed 2% handling loss, 11,221 g remains. Alternative allocations are 187 \u215? 60 g with 1 g remainder, 140 \u215? 80 g with 21 g remainder, 37 \u215? 300 g with 121 g remainder, or 22 \u215? 500 g with 221 g remainder. These are alternatives, not simultaneous outputs.\par \pard\sa120 For a 500 g loaf, arrange five 100 g balls; for a three-strand braid, use 167 + 167 + 166 g. A brioche \u224? t\u234?te may reserve about one fifth for its head. Trial small pieces at 170\u8211?180\u176?C for 14\u8211?20 minutes, 300 g loaves at 165\u8211?175\u176?C for 22\u8211?30 minutes, and 500 g loaves at 165\u8211?175\u176?C for 30\u8211?40 minutes. Confirm crumb set and measured bake loss; the 90\u8211?94\u176?C crumb target is a quality check, not a substitute for a validated food-safety process. Raw egg wash is applied only before baking.\par \pard\sa120 Cool plain brioche completely before bagging. A frozen-quality trial at \u8722?18\u176?C may compare two- and four-week samples; this does not establish a selling period or validate freezing raw dough. Keep butter, egg wash, refrigeration, rejects and unsold portions in the cost model.\par }